# Where the runner + BugReporter CLI should create bug pieces.
#
# Copy this file to config/bug_destination.yml in the project where the runner
# runs and fill in epic_relative_id. The file is gitignored — each host keeps
# its own copy and edits are never committed.
#
# epic_relative_id is the numeric id of an existing Epic piece in the same
# mcptask.online account as the runner (see CLAUDE.md → account_code). Find it
# in the URL when viewing the Epic: /pieces/<account>/<relative_id>.
#
# Why route bugs into an Epic instead of the project root?
# - Epics have no capacity limit; tasks created at the project root compete with
#   the user's regular backlog and quickly starve it.
# - Keeping auto-detected failures in one place makes triage easier (one card,
#   one assignee, one place to clear when the run is healthy again).
#
# The Installer (`rake mcptask_runner:install`) writes this file for you after
# asking which Epic to use. Re-run it with FORCE=1 to overwrite the existing
# destination. Delete the file to revert to project-root placement.
epic_relative_id: 12345   # ← replace with your Epic's relative_id
epic_name: "Auto-bugs"    # optional label, surfaced in boot banner + bug piece